eslint/no-duplicate-case Correctness ​✅ This rule is turned on by default. What it does ​Disallow duplicate case labelsWhy is this bad? ​If a switch statement has duplicate test expressions in case clauses, it is likely that a programmer copied a case clause but forgot to change the test expression.Examples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:jsvar a = 1, one = 1;
switch (a) {
  case 1:
    break;
  case 2:
    break;
  case 1: // duplicate test expression
    break;
  default:
    break;
}

switch (a) {
  case one:
    break;
  case 2:
    break;
  case one: // duplicate test expression
    break;
  default:
    break;
}Examples of correct code for this rule:jsvar a = 1,
  one = 1;
switch (a) {
  case 1:
    break;
  case 2:
    break;
  default:
    break;
}

switch (a) {
  case "1":
    break;
  case "2":
    break;
  default:
    break;
}How to use ​To enable this rule in the CLI or using the config file, you can use:CLIConfig (.oxlintrc.json)bashoxlint --deny no-duplicate-casejson{
  "rules": {
    "no-duplicate-case": "error"
  }
}References ​Rule Source

