eslint/no-global-assign Correctness ​✅ This rule is turned on by default. What it does ​Disallow modifications to read-only global variables.Why is this bad? ​In almost all cases, you don’t want to assign a value to these global variables as doing so could result in losing access to important functionality.Examples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:javascriptObject = null;How to use ​To enable this rule in the CLI or using the config file, you can use:CLIConfig (.oxlintrc.json)bashoxlint --deny no-global-assignjson{
