eslint/no-nonoctal-decimal-escape Correctness ​✅ This rule is turned on by default. 🚧 An auto-fix is still under development. What it does ​This rule disallows \8 and \9 escape sequences in string literalsWhy is this bad? ​ECMAScript specification treats \8 and \9 in string literals as a legacy featureExamples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:javascriptlet x = "\8";
let y = "\9";Examples of correct code for this rule:javascriptlet x = "8";
