eslint/no-with Correctness ​✅ This rule is turned on by default. What it does ​Disallow with statementsWhy is this bad? ​The with statement is potentially problematic because it adds members of an object to the current scope, making it impossible to tell what a variable inside the block actually refers to.Examples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:javascriptwith (point) {
    r = Math.sqrt(x * x + y * y); // is r a member of point?
}How to use ​To enable this rule in the CLI or using the config file, you can use:CLIConfig (.oxlintrc.json)bashoxlint --deny no-withjson{
    "rules": {
        "no-with": "error"
    }
}References ​Rule Source

