jest/valid-title Correctness ​🛠️ An auto-fix is available for this rule for some violations. What it does ​Checks that the titles of Jest blocks are valid.Titles must be:not empty,strings,not prefixed with their block name,have no leading or trailing spaces.Why is this bad? ​Titles that are not valid can be misleading and make it harder to understand the purpose of the test.Examples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:javascriptdescribe("", () => {});
