jsdoc/implements-on-classes Correctness ​What it does ​Reports an issue with any non-constructor function using @implements.Why is this bad? ​Constructor functions should be whether marked with @class, @constructs, or being an ES6 class constructor.Examples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:javascript/**
