react/jsx-no-duplicate-props Correctness ​What it does ​This rule prevents duplicate props in JSX elements.Why is this bad? ​Having duplicate props in a JSX element is most likely a mistake. Creating JSX elements with duplicate props can cause unexpected behavior in your application.Examples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:jsx<App a a />;
<App foo={2} bar baz foo={3} />;Examples of correct code for this rule:jsx<App a />;
<App bar baz foo={3} />;How to use ​To enable this rule in the CLI or using the config file, you can use:CLIConfig (.oxlintrc.json)bashoxlint --deny react/jsx-no-duplicate-props --react-pluginjson{
