}References ​Rule Source

typescript/no-duplicate-type-constituents Correctness ​✅ This rule is turned on by default. 💭 This rule requires type information. 🚧 An auto-fix is still under development. What it does ​This rule disallows duplicate constituents of union or intersection types.Why is this bad? ​Duplicate constituents in union and intersection types serve no purpose and can make code harder to read. They are likely a mistake.Examples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:tstype T1 = "A" | "A";

