oxc/approx-constant Suspicious ​What it does ​Disallows the use of approximate constants, instead preferring the use of the constants in the Math object.Why is this bad? ​Approximate constants are not as accurate as the constants in the Math object.Examples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:javascriptlet log10e = 0.434294;Examples of correct code for this rule:javascriptlet log10e = Math.LOG10E;How to use ​To enable this rule in the CLI or using the config file, you can use:CLIConfig (.oxlintrc.json)bashoxlint --deny oxc/approx-constantjson{
