oxc/misrefactored-assign-op Suspicious ​🚧 An auto-fix is still under development. What it does ​https://rust-lang.github.io/rust-clippy/master/#/misrefactored_assign_opChecks for a op= a op b or a op= b op a patterns.Why is this bad? ​Most likely these are bugs where one meant to write a op= b.Examples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:javascripta += a + b;
a -= a - b;Examples of correct code for this rule:javascripta += b;
a -= b;How to use ​To enable this rule in the CLI or using the config file, you can use:CLIConfig (.oxlintrc.json)bashoxlint --deny oxc/misrefactored-assign-opjson{
