typescript/no-unnecessary-type-assertion Suspicious ​💭 This rule requires type information. 🚧 An auto-fix is still under development. What it does ​This rule disallows type assertions that do not change the type of an expression.Why is this bad? ​Type assertions that don't actually change the type of an expression are unnecessary and can be safely removed. They add visual noise without providing any benefit and may indicate confusion about TypeScript's type system.Examples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:tsconst str: string = "hello";
