eslint/no-new-wrappers Pedantic ​🛠️ An auto-fix is available for this rule. What it does ​Disallow new operators with the String, Number, and Boolean objectsWhy is this bad? ​The first problem is that primitive wrapper objects are, in fact, objects. That means typeof will return "object" instead of "string", "number", or "boolean". The second problem comes with boolean objects. Every object is truthy, that means an instance of Boolean always resolves to true even when its actual value is false.https://eslint.org/docs/latest/rules/no-new-wrappersExamples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:jsvar stringObject = new String("Hello world");
var numberObject = new Number(33);
var booleanObject = new Boolean(false);
var symbolObject = new Symbol("foo"); // symbol is not a constructorExamples of correct code for this rule:jsvar stringObject = "Hello world";
var stringObject2 = String(value);
var numberObject = Number(value);
var booleanObject = Boolean(value);
var symbolObject = Symbol("foo");How to use ​To enable this rule in the CLI or using the config file, you can use:CLIConfig (.oxlintrc.json)bashoxlint --deny no-new-wrappersjson{
  "rules": {
    "no-new-wrappers": "error"
  }
}References ​Rule Source

