eslint/no-object-constructor Pedantic ​🚧 An auto-fix is still under development. What it does ​Disallow calls to the Object constructor without an argumentWhy is this bad? ​Use of the Object constructor to construct a new empty object is generally discouraged in favor of object literal notation because of conciseness and because the Object global may be redefined. The exception is when the Object constructor is used to intentionally wrap a specified value which is passed as an argument.Examples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:jsObject();
new Object();Examples of correct code for this rule:jsObject("foo");
