typescript/prefer-enum-initializers Pedantic ​🚧 An auto-fix is still under development. What it does ​Require each enum member value to be explicitly initialized.Why is this bad? ​In projects where the value of enum members are important, allowing implicit values for enums can cause bugs if enums are modified over time.Examples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:typescript// wrong, the value of `Close` is not constant
enum Status {
  Open = 1,
  Close,
}Examples of correct code for this rule:typescriptenum Status {
  Open = 1,
  Close = 2,
}How to use ​To enable this rule in the CLI or using the config file, you can use:CLIConfig (.oxlintrc.json)bashoxlint --deny typescript/prefer-enum-initializersjson{
  "rules": {
    "typescript/prefer-enum-initializers": "error"
  }
}References ​Rule Source

