unicorn/escape-case Pedantic ​🛠️ An auto-fix is available for this rule. What it does ​Enforces defining escape sequence values with uppercase characters rather than lowercase ones. This promotes readability by making the escaped value more distinguishable from the identifier.Why is this bad? ​Using lowercase characters in escape sequences makes them less readable and harder to distinguish from surrounding code. Most style guides recommend uppercase for consistency and clarity.Examples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:javascriptconst foo = "\xa9";
