unicorn/no-typeof-undefined Pedantic ​🚧 An auto-fix is still under development. What it does ​Disallow typeof comparisons with undefined.Why is this bad? ​Checking if a value is undefined by using typeof value === 'undefined' is needlessly verbose. It's generally better to compare against undefined directly. The only time typeof is needed is when a global variable potentially does not exists, in which case, using globalThis.value === undefined may be better.Examples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:javascripttypeof foo === "undefined";Examples of correct code for this rule:javascriptfoo === undefined;How to use ​To enable this rule in the CLI or using the config file, you can use:CLIConfig (.oxlintrc.json)bashoxlint --deny unicorn/no-typeof-undefinedjson{
  "rules": {
    "unicorn/no-typeof-undefined": "error"
  }
}References ​Rule Source

unicorn/no-unnecessary-array-flat-depth Pedantic ​🚧 An auto-fix is still under development. What it does ​Disallows passing 1 to Array.prototype.flatWhy is this bad? ​Passing 1 is unnecessary.Examples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:jsfoo.flat(1);Examples of correct code for this rule:jsfoo.flat();How to use ​To enable this rule in the CLI or using the config file, you can use:CLIConfig (.oxlintrc.json)bashoxlint --deny unicorn/no-unnecessary-array-flat-depthjson{
