eslint/no-label-var Style ​What it does ​Disallow labels that share a name with a variable.Why is this bad? ​This rule aims to create clearer code by disallowing the bad practice of creating a label that shares a name with a variable that is in scope.Examples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:jsvar x = foo;
function bar() {
  x:
  for (;;) {
    break x;
  }
}Examples of correct code for this rule:js// The variable that has the same name as the label is not in scope.

