eslint/no-lone-blocks Style ​What it does ​Disallows unnecessary standalone block statements.Why is this bad? ​Standalone blocks can be confusing as they do not provide any meaningful purpose when used unnecessarily. They may introduce extra nesting, reducing code readability, and can mislead readers about scope or intent.Examples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:js{
