eslint/vars-on-top Style ​What it does ​Enforces that all var declarations are placed at the top of their containing scope.Why is this bad? ​In JavaScript, var declarations are hoisted to the top of their containing scope. Placing var declarations at the top explicitly improves code readability and maintainability by making the scope of variables clear.Examples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:jsfunction doSomething() {
