jest/max-nested-describe Style ​What it does ​This rule enforces a maximum depth to nested describe() calls.Why is this bad? ​Nesting describe() blocks too deeply can make the test suite hard to read and understand.Example ​The following patterns are considered warnings (with the default option of { "max": 5 }):/// /// Examples of incorrect code for this rule:javascriptdescribe("foo", () => {
