jest/padding-around-test-blocks Style ​🛠️ An auto-fix is available for this rule. What it does ​This rule enforces a line of padding before and after 1 or more test/it statementsExamples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:jsconst thing = 123;
test("foo", () => {});
test("bar", () => {});jsconst thing = 123;
it("foo", () => {});
it("bar", () => {});Examples of correct code for this rule:jsconst thing = 123;

test("foo", () => {});

test("bar", () => {});jsconst thing = 123;

it("foo", () => {});

it("bar", () => {});How to use ​To enable this rule in the CLI or using the config file, you can use:CLIConfig (.oxlintrc.json)bashoxlint --deny jest/padding-around-test-blocks --jest-pluginjson{
  "plugins": ["jest"],
  "rules": {
