promise/prefer-await-to-then Style ​What it does ​Prefer await to then()/catch()/finally() for reading Promise valuesWhy is this bad? ​Async/await syntax can be seen as more readable.Examples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:javascriptfunction foo() {
  hey.then(x => {});
}Examples of correct code for this rule:javascriptasync function hi() {
  await thing();
}Example with strict mode ​Examples of incorrect code with { strict: true }:javascriptasync function hi() {
  await thing().then(x => {});
}How to use ​To enable this rule in the CLI or using the config file, you can use:CLIConfig (.oxlintrc.json)bashoxlint --deny promise/prefer-await-to-then --promise-pluginjson{
  "plugins": ["promise"],
  "rules": {
