unicorn/no-await-expression-member Style ​⚠️🛠️️ A dangerous auto-fix is available for this rule. What it does ​Disallows member access from await expressions.Why is this bad? ​When accessing a member from an await expression, the await expression has to be parenthesized, which is not readable.Examples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:javascriptasync function bad() {
  const secondElement = (await getArray())[1];
}Examples of correct code for this rule:javascriptasync function good() {
  const [, secondElement] = await getArray();
}How to use ​To enable this rule in the CLI or using the config file, you can use:CLIConfig (.oxlintrc.json)bashoxlint --deny unicorn/no-await-expression-memberjson{
  "rules": {
    "unicorn/no-await-expression-member": "error"
  }
}References ​Rule Source

