unicorn/prefer-spread Style ​🛠️ An auto-fix is available for this rule for some violations. What it does ​Enforces the use of the spread operator (...) over outdated patterns.Why is this bad? ​Using the spread operator is more concise and readable.Examples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:javascriptconst foo = Array.from(set);
const foo = Array.from(new Set([1, 2]));Examples of correct code for this rule:javascript[...set].map(() => {});
Array.from(...argumentsArray);How to use ​To enable this rule in the CLI or using the config file, you can use:CLIConfig (.oxlintrc.json)bashoxlint --deny unicorn/prefer-spreadjson{
