}References ​Rule Source

unicorn/prefer-string-raw Style ​🛠️ An auto-fix is available for this rule. What it does ​Prefers use of String.raw to avoid escaping .Why is this bad? ​Excessive backslashes can make string values less readable which can be avoided by using String.raw.Examples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:javascriptconst file = "C:\\windows\\style\\path\\to\\file.js";
const regexp = new RegExp("foo\\.bar");Examples of correct code for this rule:javascriptconst file = String.raw`C:\windows\style\path\to\file.js`;
const regexp = new RegExp(String.raw`foo\.bar`);How to use ​To enable this rule in the CLI or using the config file, you can use:CLIConfig (.oxlintrc.json)bashoxlint --deny unicorn/prefer-string-rawjson{
