    "unicorn/prefer-structured-clone": "error"
  }
}References ​Rule Source

unicorn/require-array-join-separator Style ​🛠️ An auto-fix is available for this rule for some violations. What it does ​Enforce using the separator argument with Array#join()Why is this bad? ​It's better to make it clear what the separator is when calling Array#join(), instead of relying on the default comma (',') separator.Examples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:javascriptfoo.join();Examples of correct code for this rule:javascriptfoo.join(",");How to use ​To enable this rule in the CLI or using the config file, you can use:CLIConfig (.oxlintrc.json)bashoxlint --deny unicorn/require-array-join-separatorjson{
