  }
}References ​Rule Source

vitest/prefer-to-be-object Style ​🛠️ An auto-fix is available for this rule. What it does ​This rule enforces using toBeObject() to check if a value is of type Object.Why is this bad? ​Using other methods such as toBeInstanceOf(Object) or instanceof Object can be less clear and potentially misleading. Enforcing the use of toBeObject() provides more explicit and readable code, making your intentions clear and improving the overall maintainability and readability of your tests.Examples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:jsexpectTypeOf({}).toBeInstanceOf(Object);
expectTypeOf({} instanceof Object).toBeTruthy();Examples of correct code for this rule:jsexpectTypeOf({}).toBeObject();
expectTypeOf({}).toBeObject();How to use ​To enable this rule in the CLI or using the config file, you can use:CLIConfig (.oxlintrc.json)bashoxlint --deny vitest/prefer-to-be-object --vitest-pluginjson{
