vue/define-emits-declaration Style ​🚧 An auto-fix is still under development. What it does ​This rule enforces defineEmits typing style which you should use type-based, strict type-literal (introduced in Vue 3.3), or runtime declaration. This rule only works in setup script and lang="ts".Examples ​Examples of incorrect code for this rule:vue// "vue/define-emits-declaration": ["error", "type-based"]
